module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.HomogeneousLineBundleSections
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.RhoRegularWeylOrbit
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.BorelSimpleRootDistributionCalculus

/-! # Infinitesimal invariants of restricted induced modules

Source: Mathieu, Tilting Modules and their Applications (2000), Lemmas 2.1 and 2.3,
printed pp.153--155 (blueprint: lem-sfb-restricted-induced-infinitesimal-invariants).

The module is the actual global sections of the associated homogeneous line bundle.
A finite basis describes its rational left-translation action, pinned by evaluation
on every algebra-valued point. Its infinitesimal action is the existing differential
of that representation composed with the inclusion of the unipotent radical.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory CartesianMonoidalCategory
open scoped MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A restricted dominant induced module has exactly its highest-weight line as
its infinitesimal unipotent invariants. The same nonzero vector is fixed by the
whole unipotent group scheme and has torus character λ.

Source: Mathieu, Lemma 2.3, second assertion, printed p.155; Lemma 2.1,
printed pp.153--154 (blueprint: lem-sfb-restricted-induced-infinitesimal-invariants).

Conventions: χ = w₀λ extended along πT, so the presentation L_χ is M_{-w₀λ}.
The inverse character ψ gives its positive-right-semi-invariant function model.
The equivalence e is normalized by pullback in the presentation's trivialization.
The basis d and rational representation r satisfy the left-translation identity,
so the displayed differential is the specified differentiated action on sections.

Proof plan:
1. Use lem-sfb-induced-dual-lowest-distribution-generator to obtain finite
   nonzero V and a dual generator w, killed by the simple divided powers above
   the simple coroot pairings. The comparison
   lem-sfb-homogeneous-line-bundle-sections identifies V with E_B(w₀λ).
   By lem-sfb-induced-module-primitive-line its group-scheme U-fixed line has
   weight w₀(w₀λ) = λ, using lem-sfb-rho-regular-weyl-orbit.
2. In lem-sfb-borel-simple-root-distribution-calculus write H = Dist(U) and A
   for the subalgebra generated by Lie(U). For Z = Aw the adjoint coefficient
   identity expands D_i^(n) a w into C_i,r(a) D_i^(b) w. Terms b ≥ p vanish
   since the pairings are < p. For b < p both factors belong to A. Thus Z is
   stable under all divided powers, which generate H, so V dual = Hw = Aw.
3. The quotient of V dual by Lie(U) times V dual is spanned by the class of w:
   every positive-length word in Lie(U) lies in that subspace. Under the
   contragredient identity (xℓ)(v) = -ℓ(xv), Lie-invariant vectors identify
   with its annihilator, of dimension at most one. Linear forms separate
   vectors. Differentiating the nonzero group-fixed vector from step 1 puts
   that vector in the annihilator, proving equality with its span. Its
   U-fixity and torus character are those of step 1. For S = 1 this gives
   V = F and includes λ = 0; no nonempty-root hypothesis is imposed. -/
theorem restricted_induced_infinitesimal_invariants
    {F : Type u} [Field F] [IsAlgClosed F] (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] [CharP F p]
    (S T B U : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (hS : IsSemisimpleGroupScheme S.X)
    (hsc : ∀ (S' : Over (Spec (.of F))) [GrpObj S'],
      IsSemisimpleGroupScheme S' → ∀ (f : S' ⟶ S.X) [IsMonHom f],
      Surjective f.left → IsFinite (GrpObj.ker f).hom →
      (∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra F A]
        (x : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ GrpObj.ker f)
        (s : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ S'),
        (x ≫ GrpObj.kerι f) * s = s * (x ≫ GrpObj.kerι f)) → IsIso f)
    (iT : T ⟶ S) (iB : B ⟶ S) (j : T ⟶ B) (hj : j ≫ iB = iT)
    (hT : ReductiveTorusCentralizer.IsMaximalTorus iT)
    (hsplit : ∃ n : ℕ, Nonempty (T ≅ MultiplicativeType.splitTorus F n))
    (hB : IsBorelGroupScheme iB.hom.hom)
    (iU : U ⟶ B)
    (hU : IsClosedSubgroupScheme iU.hom.hom ∧ IsNormalSubgroupScheme iU.hom.hom ∧
      Smooth U.X.hom ∧ ConnectedSpace U.X.left ∧ SolvableGroupStructure.IsUnipotent U ∧
      ∀ (N : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iN : N ⟶ B),
        IsClosedSubgroupScheme iN.hom.hom → IsNormalSubgroupScheme iN.hom.hom →
        Smooth N.X.hom → ConnectedSpace N.X.left → SolvableGroupStructure.IsUnipotent N →
        ∃ f : N ⟶ U, f ≫ iU = iN)
    (πT : B ⟶ T) (hπT : j ≫ πT = 𝟙 T)
    (hker : IsPullback iU.hom.hom (toUnit U.X) πT.hom.hom η[T.X])
    (hsd : IsIso ((fst U.X T.X ≫ iU.hom.hom) * (snd U.X T.X ≫ j.hom.hom)))
    [IsCommMonObj T.X] [IsCommMonObj (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)]
    (aS : ModObj T.X S.X) (aB : ModObj T.X B.X)
    (Φ : Finset (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F))))
    (P : RootDatum Φ
      (Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
      (Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)))
    (b : P.Base) [P.IsReduced]
    (hconjS : aS.smul = (iT.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 S.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj S.X)
    (hconjB : aB.smul = (j.hom.hom ⊗ₘ 𝟙 B.X) ≫ GrpObj.conj B.X)
    (hroot : ∀ α : Φ, P.root α = α.val)
    (hpair : ∀ (χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
      (ν : Additive (Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F) ⟶ T)),
      ν.toMul.hom.hom ≫ χ.toMul.hom.hom =
        (𝟙 (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)) ^ (P.toLinearMap χ ν))
    (hweights : ∀ χ : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)),
      χ ∈ Φ ↔ χ ≠ 0 ∧ @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T S aS χ.toMul ≠ ⊥)
    (hpos : ∀ α : Φ, b.IsPos α ↔
      @TorusCharacterTangent.weightSpace F _ T B aB α.val.toMul ≠ ⊥)
    (act : RankOneRoots.Weyl iT →* Aut T)
    (hact : ∀ (n : RankOneRoots.normalizer iT) (A : CommAlgCat.{u} F)
      (t : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ T.X),
      t ≫ (act (QuotientGroup.mk n)).hom.hom.hom ≫ iT.hom.hom =
        (toUnit (StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A) ≫ n.val) * (t ≫ iT.hom.hom) *
          (toUnit (StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A) ≫ n.val)⁻¹)
    (w₀ : RankOneRoots.Weyl iT)
    (hw₀ : Set.image (fun α : Φ ↦ Additive.ofMul ((act w₀).inv ≫ α.val.toMul))
      {α : Φ | b.IsPos α} = Set.image (fun α : Φ ↦ -α.val) {α : Φ | b.IsPos α})
    (lam : Additive (T ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F)))
    (hlam : ∀ α ∈ b.support,
      0 ≤ P.toLinearMap lam (P.coroot α) ∧ P.toLinearMap lam (P.coroot α) < (p : ℤ))
    (Q : Over (Spec (.of F))) (π : S.X ⟶ Q)
    (hQ : IsProper Q.hom) (hQft : LocallyOfFiniteType Q.hom) (hQqc : QuasiCompact Q.hom)
    (hπf : Flat π.left) (hπs : Surjective π.left)
    (hπi : (fst S.X B.X * (snd S.X B.X ≫ iB.hom.hom)) ≫ π = fst S.X B.X ≫ π)
    (hπt : IsPullback (fst S.X B.X)
      (fst S.X B.X * (snd S.X B.X ≫ iB.hom.hom)) π π)
    (χ ψ : B ⟶ Grp.mk (StandardGroupSchemes.multiplicative F))
    (hχ : χ = πT ≫ (act w₀).inv ≫ lam.toMul) (hψ : ψ.hom.hom = χ.hom.hom⁻¹)
    (L : AssociatedCharacterLineBundle.Presentation S B iB Q π χ) :
    Module.Finite F (AssociatedCharacterLineBundle.sections Q L.L) ∧
    ∃ e : AssociatedCharacterLineBundle.sections Q L.L ≃ₗ[F]
      RhoSection.sectionModule S B iB ψ 1,
      (∀ σ : AssociatedCharacterLineBundle.sections Q L.L,
        (e σ).val = AssociatedCharacterLineBundle.pullbackCoordinate π L.L L.trivialization σ) ∧
      ∃ (I : Type u) (_ : Fintype I) (_ : DecidableEq I)
        (d : (I → F) ≃ₗ[F] AssociatedCharacterLineBundle.sections Q L.L)
        (r : GeneralLinearGroup.RationalHom S.X I) (_ : IsMonHom r),
        (∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra F A]
          (s g : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ S.X) (k : I),
          ∑ l, (r.points A s : Matrix I I A) l k *
            RhoSection.evaluate g (e (d (Pi.single l 1))).val =
              RhoSection.evaluate (s⁻¹ * g) (e (d (Pi.single k 1))).val) ∧
        ∃ v : AssociatedCharacterLineBundle.sections Q L.L,
          v ≠ 0 ∧
          (∀ w : AssociatedCharacterLineBundle.sections Q L.L,
            (∀ x : GrpObj.Lie U.X,
              (r.differential (GrpObj.differential (iU ≫ iB).hom.hom x)).mulVec (d.symm w) = 0)
                ↔ w ∈ Submodule.span F {v}) ∧
          (∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra F A]
            (a : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ U.X),
            (r.points A (a ≫ iU.hom.hom ≫ iB.hom.hom) : Matrix I I A).mulVec
              (fun k ↦ algebraMap F A (d.symm v k)) =
                fun k ↦ algebraMap F A (d.symm v k)) ∧
          (∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra F A]
            (t : StandardGroupSchemes.affine F A ⟶ T.X),
            (r.points A (t ≫ iT.hom.hom) : Matrix I I A).mulVec
              (fun k ↦ algebraMap F A (d.symm v k)) =
                RhoSection.characterValue (t ≫ lam.toMul.hom.hom) •
                  (fun k ↦ algebraMap F A (d.symm v k))) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
